<title>GERMANY: Dresdner 96 net profit up 30.7 pct.</title>
<headline>Dresdner 96 net profit up 30.7 pct.</headline>
<dateline>FRANKFURT 1997-04-10</dateline>
<text>
<p>Calendar 1996</p>
<p>(in millions of marks unless otherwise stated)</p>
<p>    Group net profit			    1,580  vs 1,209</p>
<p>    Group oper profit after provisions    2,866  vs 1,992</p>
<p>    Group loan loss provisions		1,102  vs 1,075</p>
<p>    Group own account trading income	666.5  vs 593</p>
<p>    Group net interest income		 6,920  vs 6,321</p>
<p>    Group net commission income	     4,129  vs 3,047</p>
<p>    Group administration costs		8,537  vs 7,260</p>
<p>    Allocation to earnings reserves	 812.9  vs 570.6</p>
<p>    Capital ratio  (BIS)			9.4    vs 9.7 pct</p>
<p>    DVFA earnings per share		   2.87   vs 2.64 dmk</p>
<p>    Dividend (already announced)	    1.45   vs 1.35 dmk</p>
<p>    Bonus dividend				0.10   vs n/a dmk</p>
<p>    Balance sheet total		     561,163  vs 484,482</p>
<p>    Lending volume			    322,791  vs 285,985</p>
<p>NOTE - Full name of the German bank is Dresdner Bank AG.</p>
<p>The bank had already reported estimated operating profit and its dividend. Analysts had forecast Dresdner's net profit at around 1.57 billion marks. The bonus dividend is to mark the bank's 125th anniversary.</p>
<p>--Frankfurt Newsroom, +49 69 756525</p>
</text>
